# Documentation maintenance

This project keeps durable context in `docs/` because chats do not persist across sessions.

## Doc map

- `docs/overview.md` — purpose, features, build/install, layout
- `docs/design.md` — UI/UX (status item + popover)
- `docs/architecture.md` — tech stack, auth, APIs, data flow
- `docs/README.md` — index / quick start

## When to update

After any meaningful change, update the matching doc in the **same task**:

- Status bar copy, spacing, divider, colors, hover/click behavior → `docs/design.md`
- Popover layout, meters, labels, what `%` means → `docs/design.md`
- Endpoints, auth files, polling, models, packaging → `docs/architecture.md`
- Features list, install path, requirements → `docs/overview.md`

## Rules for writing

- Document what the code **actually** does; do not invent APIs or fields
- Prefer short, concrete bullets over long prose
- Call out unofficial endpoints and known caveats (especially Cursor Auto vs Other Models)
- Do not put secrets, tokens, or raw `auth.json` contents into docs
